  "note": "Roman to Tirhuta (Mithilakshar) for Maithili. Tirhuta is a Devanagari-shaped abugida with its own virama and vowel signs, so this map reuses the reviewed Devanagari romanisation keys one-for-one against Tirhuta letters rather than inventing a second convention. The danda and double danda are not reproduced: Tirhuta shares Devanagari's, and a Tirhuta map must not emit Devanagari. UNVERIFIED ASSUMPTION: the romanisation keys are Nepali's. Nepal Bhasa's reviewed Roman pack uses a different convention from Nepali for the same Devanagari script (its 'ch' is CHA where Nepali's is CA), so languages sharing a script demonstrably do not share a romanisation. No evidence was found that Maithili speakers use the Nepali convention. The letter-to-letter script correspondence is sound and cross-checked against the Deva-to-Tirhuta converter; it is the choice of Roman keys that needs a Maithili speaker.",
